# Local VS Code settings (per-window theme override, etc.) — not for readers.
.vscode/

# Personal VS Code workspace file (may carry local theme/settings) — not for readers.
*.code-workspace

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No binaries. This repo is public and ships SOURCE ONLY.
#
# Tools are installed by the reader from their own release — sqlsim comes from
# https://aka.ms/sqlsimtools (see the Chapter 2 Prerequisites section). A
# vendored binary goes stale against the book's text, cannot be reviewed in a
# diff, and has no business in a public Microsoft repo.
#
# Files arrive here via tools/publish-examples.ps1 in the authoring repo, which
# refuses to copy anything matching this list. These rules are the second line
# of defence, for the case where a file is dropped in by hand.
#
# Figures (*.png, *.svg) are binary-ish but ARE source, so they are not listed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.exe
*.com
*.msi
*.msix
*.appx
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.a
*.lib
*.pdb
*.nupkg
*.jar
*.class
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.*
*.tgz
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz
